}, "features": ["option_type", "log_forward_moneyness", "total_volatility", "rate_time", "yield_time"], "git_commit": "fefcc3b96a8b94588c5921590af507372569f803", "hypothesis": "E2 failed to learn because its loss was differentiated through a saturated smooth-floor projection, not because the floor itself is incompatible with price accuracy; computing the same loss on the pre-projection direct value, while evaluating and deploying the floored output unchanged, recovers the direct residual model's price accuracy and keeps the intrinsic and analytic-European bounds enforced.", "interpretation": "E2b confirmed that E2 failed because training gradients were routed through the saturated floor. Training the latent residual network on the direct normalized-price target while evaluating the identical floored output passed all three price gates: RMSE 0.0013192586235663635, p99 0.005480095733763145 and maximum 0.01900577580721763. It enforced the intrinsic floor and observed materially better price accuracy than the direct residual run, but retained 4135 CRR-European comparator violations and 532 shape violations: 57 spot-monotonicity, 271 spot-convexity and 204 volatility-monotonicity. The remaining decision is no longer architectural price fitting; it is whether the non-deployable CRR comparator mismatch should block E3 shape treatment.", "next_action": "change-direction obtain independent scientific advice before E3 on the CRR-versus-analytic-European gate mismatch, shape treatment and latency priority", "optimizer_and_budget": {"batch_size": 2048, "beta1": 0.9, "beta2": 0.999, "deterministic_algorithms": true, "epochs": 120, "epsilon": 1e-08, "learning_rate": 0.001, "minimum_learning_rate": 0.0, "name": "adamw", "num_threads": 4, "schedule": "cosine_annealing", "schedule_period_epochs": 120, "shuffle": "torch.randperm from the shuffle seed once per epoch", "weight_decay": 1e-06}, "outcome": "criterion_not_met", "parent_attempt": "scratch_residual_smooth_floor_v1", "price_m